# US-0072 (EPIC-0003 voice A1c): the TLS proxy of deploy/compose/voice.yml (profile `lan`). One hostname and one owner-supplied
# certificate, two sites: the web app on VOICE_HTTPS_PORT and LiveKit signalling on VOICE_LIVEKIT_TLS_PORT.
#
# - No log directive anywhere: the LiveKit token travels in the signalling URL's query, so an access log would record it.
# - No trusted_proxies and no header directive for X-Forwarded-For: Caddy then REPLACES that header with the client's own address,
#   which the web app's throttles rely on (docs/THREAT_MODEL.md, "Client address, TRUST_PROXY and the per-role throttles").
# - The LiveKit site forwards only /rtc* (signalling and validation) and drops the Cookie header: the __Host-scenecoach cookie is sent
#   to every port of the host, and LiveKit's HTTP port also serves its server API. Everything else answers 404.
# - admin off (no admin endpoint); HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 only (UDP is not published, so no HTTP/3); no port 80 redirect server.
{
	admin off
	auto_https disable_redirects
	servers {
		protocols h1 h2
	}
}

{$VOICE_HOSTNAME}:{$VOICE_HTTPS_PORT} {
	tls /certs/cert.pem /certs/key.pem
	reverse_proxy {$VOICE_WEB_UPSTREAM}
}

{$VOICE_HOSTNAME}:{$VOICE_LIVEKIT_TLS_PORT} {
	tls /certs/cert.pem /certs/key.pem
	handle /rtc* {
		reverse_proxy livekit:7880 {
			header_up -Cookie
		}
	}
	handle {
		respond 404
	}
}
